{{firstName}},

Most retained-search founders are running a high-paying job, not a business. {Every search comes from your network.|Every meeting traces back to someone you know.} The firm has your name on it but runs on your relationships.

{Works fine until two things happen at once|Fine until two things go wrong at the same time} - a big client pauses hiring, and your network has nothing new in it.

I build the system that fills the calendar {without your personal involvement|hands-off for you|that doesn't need you to be the rainmaker}.

{Want a quick map of how this works for retained search specifically?|Mind if I send something useful instead of a pitch?|Want me to put a sample together for {{companyName}}?}

{{senderFirst}}

{{firstName}},

{Spent 20 min on {{companyName}} this morning.|Took a quick look at {{companyName}} this morning.|Looked through {{companyName}} this morning.}

{If it's useful|If it'd help|If this is interesting}, I can pull 20 verified contacts in your ICP - Heads of People / CHROs at companies actively scaling - and send them over. {Yours whether we work together or not.|Yours regardless.|Free, no strings.}

Takes me an hour. No pitch, just the list.

{Want me to put it together for {{companyName}}?|Should I pull the 20 and send them?|Mind if I send the sample?}

{{senderFirst}}

{{firstName}}, {quick add-on.|one more thought.|small follow-up.}

Counterintuitive thing about retained-search outbound: the highest-reply prospects are VPs in their first 90 days at a new role, not C-suite. {New VPs are trying to make their mark and stay open to vendors C-suite would filter out.|They're building their org and haven't built filters yet.}

Worth knowing whether you outsource outbound or do it in-house.

{{senderFirst}}

{{firstName}}, {a quick data point|sharing a number|one stat worth knowing}:

Retained-search firms running outbound at this scale typically land 2-3 qualified discovery calls per week from cold. Roughly 1 search engagement per month closes from that flow.

All from inboxes the senior team never touches.

{Want to see what that looks like for {{companyName}}?|Worth a quick walkthrough?|Open to seeing how this would work?}

{{senderFirst}}

{{firstName}}, {last attempt.|honest question.|one more.}

Is filling the search pipeline something {{companyName}} is actively working on, or is it sorted for now?

Either answer is fine - just want to know if I should follow up later.

{{senderFirst}}

{{firstName}}, {closing the loop here.|stepping back.|done following up.}

{Not going to push further.|Won't keep nudging.} If retained-search prospect flow ever comes up for {{companyName}}, you have my email.

{Best with the practice.|Good luck with the year.|Wishing you a strong year.}

